What:           /sys/class/amhdmitx/amhdmitx0/vid_mute_kodi
Date:           October 2026
Contact:        p3i maintainers
Description:
                Dedicated boolean video-mute request for a single Kodi instance.
                Write 1 to hold or 0 to release; repeated writes are idempotent.
                Input is one digit, optionally followed by a newline. Reading
                returns this slot's requested state, not physical output status.

                A new Kodi process may write 0 once before creating its holds to
                recover its predecessor's request after a crash. This does not
                release HDR's internal request or decrement references owned by
                clients of the existing vid_mute interface. Output is unmuted
                only when all three owner classes release it. The normal driver
                applies requests at vsync; the DRM variant dispatches directly.

                This is an exclusive client slot, not a per-process lease. Do
                not share it between concurrent Kodi instances or other clients.
                It does not identify or clear references leaked through legacy
                vid_mute, and does not auto-release while Kodi remains stopped.
